```

Requirements:
- Output must be valid Stim text and parse with stim.Circuit.
- Use the same qubit indexing as the baseline circuit (temporary internal relabeling is allowed only if mapped back before tool calls/final submission).
- The candidate must preserve ALL stabilizers in the target stabilizers according to evaluate_optimization (valid must be true).
- The candidate must be STRICTLY more optimal than the baseline using lexicographic order on:
   1. two_qubit_gates (primary) — total count of all two-qubit gates (CX, CZ, SWAP, etc.)
   2. volume (secondary) — total gate count in the volume gate set
   3. depth (tertiary) — circuit depth
- Do NOT introduce measurements, resets, or noise unless they already exist in the baseline and are required.
- The final submission must be a single circuit text body (no Markdown fences, no prose, no extra markers).

Optimization rule (lexicographic):
- Candidate is strictly better if:
   - cand.two_qubit_gates < base.two_qubit_gates, OR
   - cand.two_qubit_gates == base.two_qubit_gates AND cand.volume < base.volume, OR
   - cand.two_qubit_gates == base.two_qubit_gates AND cand.volume == base.volume AND cand.depth < base.depth
- If all three metrics are equal or higher, it is NOT an improvement.

Note: two_qubit_gates counts ALL two-qubit entangling gates (CX, CZ, SWAP, etc.), not just CX.
Reducing any two-qubit gate type is equally valuable since all propagate errors between qubits.

## Strategies to try (individually and optionally in combinations)
Try these as a toolbox, not a fixed single path. Use judgment to determine which strategies are valid.
- Tableau/stabilizer Gaussian-elimination-based synthesis (baseline / resynthesis)
- Reordering of stabilizer generators before synthesis
- Qubit permutation / relabeling search (random and heuristic)
- Local Clifford normalization / canonicalization before synthesis
- Graph-state / LC-equivalent transformations (if applicable), then synthesize and map back
- CNOT network resynthesis / cancellation passes
- Gate commutation + cancellation + peephole simplification
- Layering / scheduling improvements to reduce depth

Tooling / attempt-budget rules:
- You may call evaluate_optimization to test a candidate circuit. It checks BOTH stabilizer preservation AND optimization metrics in a single call.
  - The response includes 'valid' (true/false), 'preserved_stabilizers' (int), and 'better' (true/false).
  - A candidate is VALID only when valid == true (all stabilizers preserved).
  - A candidate is an IMPROVEMENT only when valid == true AND better == true.
- IMPORTANT: each candidate circuit counts as ONE attempt.
- You have a total budget of 1 attempt(s) = at most 1 calls to evaluate_optimization.
- Keep track of the best VALID candidate seen so far:
  - Valid = preserves all stabilizers (valid == true).
  - Best = strictly more optimal than the baseline by the lexicographic rule (better == true).
  - If multiple valid+better candidates found, the best is the one with the lowest (two_qubit_gates, volume, depth) tuple.
- Do NOT call or rely on repository tools besides evaluate_optimization and final_circuit.
- If you need temporary/scratch files, write them into: /home/godseye/Public/Assignments/607/stabilizer-bench/runs/smoke-004-b2-perfect5/repo/rq3/data/claude-sonnet-4-5/agent_files/261026.160931

Required workflow:
1. Start from the baseline circuit as the current reference.
2. Propose a candidate rewrite (from baseline or best-so-far).
3. Call evaluate_optimization on the candidate — this checks stabilizers AND metrics in one step (uses one attempt).
4. If valid == true AND better == true, update your best-so-far. Continue trying to improve further with remaining attempts.
5. If not valid or not better, try a different strategy.
6. You MUST stop after 1 attempts regardless.
7. After all attempts are exhausted, call final_circuit with the best valid+better candidate found.
8. If no valid+better candidate was found, still call final_circuit with the best valid candidate (the harness may reject it).

Output / submission rules:
- Do NOT output Markdown code fences, prose, or extra markers.
- When ready, call final_circuit with ONLY the raw Stim circuit text in the 'stim_circuit' field.
- Do not end the conversation without calling final_circuit.
